#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run a builder's own test, clippy or build run so that it yields to the gates.

Usage:
  factory/bin/test-run [--here] -- <command> [args...]

  --here    the run needs this Mac itself (its Keychain, the owner's real home): it runs here, under the
            lock, and goes to neither the gate VM nor the Mac worker

e.g.
  factory/bin/test-run -- cargo test -p obid --test jobs_api
  factory/bin/test-run --here -- cargo test -p obid vault::
  factory/bin/test-run -- npm test

Heavy and light. Only a run that can build Rust or Xcode code takes turns. The
command's arguments are joined with spaces and split into words on whitespace
and on ; & | ( ) < > ' " and the backquote; a word's name is the text after its
last /. The command is heavy when any word's name is cargo, cargo-nextest,
nextest, rustc, xcodebuild, oby-check.sh or oby-check-blok, or when a word's
name is swift and a later word is build or test. Matching is case-sensitive
(Cargo.toml doesn't count). So `sh -c "cargo test"`, `env X=1 cargo test`,
`/path/to/cargo clippy` and `swift test` are heavy; `python3 -m unittest`,
`npm test`, `npx vitest` and `npm run typecheck` are light. A light run starts
at once: it never opens, takes or waits for the lock, and writes no holder
line; everything below but the lock still holds for it.

Lock. One heavy run at a time on this Mac: test-run holds
~/Library/Caches/oby-factory/test-run.lock (OBY_TEST_RUN_LOCK overrides it, for
the tests only), beside the shared Cargo folder and not in it, so pruning that
folder never deletes it. It is never the gate's lock: a gate's check holds only
its own, so a gate never waits on a builder's run. The holder writes the line
`<pid> <started> <cwd> <command>` into it, <started> the UTC time it took the
lock (2026-11-14T05:04:52Z). A heavy run that finds the lock held says who
holds it once ("another test run holds the lock (<holder line>); waiting for
it") and blocks on it; while it still waits it says so again every 5 minutes,
reading the holder line afresh: "still waiting for the lock after <N> min; it
is held by (<holder line>)". OBY_TEST_RUN_REPORT_SECONDS overrides those 300
seconds, for the tests only.

Priority. The command runs at `nice -n 15`, so a gate's check, at normal
priority, gets the CPU first whenever both want it, and the run has the whole
Mac when no gate runs. Not `taskpolicy -b`: it also throttles the run's disk
I/O and keeps it on the Mac's efficiency cores even when no gate runs, which
makes a Rust build several times slower for no gain.

Cores. CARGO_BUILD_JOBS, RUST_TEST_THREADS and NEXTEST_TEST_THREADS are each
set to half the cores (at least 1); a smaller positive value the caller set is
kept. An explicit `-j` or `--test-threads` on the command line overrides them.
Commands that read none of them (npm test, npm run typecheck, swift test) are
held only by the priority (and swift test by the lock), not by a core cap. Everything else in
the environment passes through unchanged.

Build folder. A run whose CARGO_TARGET_DIR is the factory's shared Cargo folder
(CARGO_TARGET_DIR_FACTORY, else ~/Library/Caches/oby-factory/core-target, as in
factory/bin/job; compared with realpath, so a trailing / or a link counts),
heavy or light, is refused before any lock: test-run says so in one line and
exits 2 without running it. Cargo gives a workspace crate the same build record
in every worktree and finds it fresh when no source file is newer than that
build, so a crate another worktree built there can run in place of this one's.
Run with CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<worktree>/core/target instead. Any other
CARGO_TARGET_DIR, or none, passes through unchanged.

Ending. As factory/bin/check-lock, through child_session.py beside it: the
lock stays in test-run's own process and isn't inherited; the command runs as a
child in a session of its own. When it ends, or test-run gets SIGTERM or SIGINT
(while waiting for the lock too), everything still running in that session gets
SIGTERM, and test-run exits with the command's code (128 + signal when it or
test-run was stopped). The lock is released with test-run.

The gate VM (docs/contracts/remote-gate.md, REMOTE-22 to 31). With the gate's
VM settings valid (config.json's `remote_gate` in the main checkout, or
FACTORY_REMOTE_GATE) and their `builder_slots` 1 or more, a heavy run that
doesn't need macOS runs on the VM instead, before any lock; the command line
stays the same. It stays here when a word's name is swift, xcodebuild,
oby-check.sh or oby-check-blok; when the worktree's changes against its base
(git merge-base HEAD origin/<base_branch>, to the working tree: committed,
uncommitted and new files that aren't ignored) touch macOS-only code by the
gate's own rule (factory/bin/gate's MACOS_ONLY, or a file whose copy here or on
the base names target_os = "macos"); or when a `--test <name>` names such a
core/crates/*/tests/<name>.rs. Then it says `factory/bin/test-run: on this Mac:
<why>` and runs here as above.

What is sent: the base's SHA, which is on origin, and the SHA of the worktree's
tree, written from an index of its own (seeded from HEAD, then `git add -A`, so
nothing ignored is in it; the worktree's own index is untouched), and on ssh's
standard input a line with the size of `git diff --binary --full-index <base>
<tree>`, then that diff, after `gitleaks stdin` with the main checkout's
.gitleaks.toml passed it (a finding, or a scanner that can't run, keeps the run
here). Standard input then stays open until the run ends. Nothing else goes: no
environment variable, CARGO_TARGET_DIR, token, login or file. The call is `ssh
<the gate's ssh options> -l <builder_user> <ssh_host> oby-remote-gate --run
--slots <n> --builder-slots <m> --wait 600 <base> <tree> <folder> -- <command>`,
its words quoted so fish and bash read them the same (the gate's command_line),
with <folder> the run's folder in the worktree (FACTORY_BUILDER_WAIT_SECONDS
lowers the 600, for the tests only). The VM applies the diff to the base in a
builder slot of its own, checks the tree, gives every file under core/ and
tools/ the current time, and runs the command there at nice 15, offline, with
the slot's own CARGO_TARGET_DIR and its share of the VM's cores.

While it runs, test-run's use of the VM is open in the main checkout's
factory/jobs/remote-gate/state.json, as a gate's is, so `gate --idle` keeps the
VM up; the gate's reach starts a stopped VM and waits for SSH (180 seconds, then
the SSH rule follows this Mac's IP). The VM's output comes to stdout as it comes.
Once it says `oby-remote-gate: running in builder slot <N>`, ssh's exit code is
test-run's, and the command never runs here too. Before that line (the VM
unreachable or not started in time, no builder user, ssh's 255, every builder
slot busy for 600 seconds, a payload that doesn't apply), it says
`factory/bin/test-run: fell back to this Mac: <why>` and runs here as above,
lock included. SIGTERM or SIGINT stops ssh, which ends the run's session on the
VM and frees its slot, and test-run exits 128 + signal. A run whose
CARGO_TARGET_DIR is the shared folder is still refused first.

The Mac worker (REMOTE-35 to 42). With config.json's `mac_worker` (or
FACTORY_MAC_WORKER) valid and its `builder_slots` 1 or more, a heavy run that stays
here above only because of macOS-only code or a macOS-only `--test` goes to the
Mac worker instead, with or without the VM: it says `factory/bin/test-run: to the
Mac worker <host>: <why>` and sends the same base, tree, folder and scanned
payload, through `ssh <the gate's ssh options> <ssh_host> oby-worker/bin/
oby-remote-gate --mac --run --slots 2 --builder-slots <m> --wait 600 <base>
<tree> <folder> -- <command>`, its words quoted so fish and bash read them the
same, with no -l. It runs there in a builder
slot of its own under ~/oby-worker/builders, never a gate's. No use is opened in
state.json, and nothing is started or probed first. Streaming, the `running in
builder slot <N>` line, exit codes, stops and the fallback to this Mac before
that line are as for the VM. A run with a Mac word stays here, as does any run
with `--here`, which says `factory/bin/test-run: on this Mac: the run asked for
this Mac (--here)` and calls no host. A fallback from either host runs here,
never on the other. With `mac_worker` missing, invalid or its `builder_slots`
0, nothing above changes.
"""

import fcntl
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import threading
import time
from pathlib import Path

import child_session

NAME = "factory/bin/test-run"
LOCK = Path(os.environ.get("OBY_TEST_RUN_LOCK") or Path.home() / "Library/Caches/oby-factory/test-run.lock")
SHARED = Path(os.environ.get("CARGO_TARGET_DIR_FACTORY",
                             Path.home() / "Library/Caches/oby-factory/core-target"))
REPORT_SECONDS = float(os.environ.get("OBY_TEST_RUN_REPORT_SECONDS") or 300)
PRIORITY = 15
CORE_VARS = ("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS", "RUST_TEST_THREADS", "NEXTEST_TEST_THREADS")
HEAVY = {"cargo", "cargo-nextest", "nextest", "rustc", "xcodebuild", "oby-check.sh", "oby-check-blok"}
MAC_WORDS = ("swift", "xcodebuild", "oby-check.sh", "oby-check-blok")  # never sent to the gate VM
WAIT = min(600, int(os.environ.get("FACTORY_BUILDER_WAIT_SECONDS") or 600))  # lower only in the tests
FOLDER = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+")  # oby-remote-gate's rule for the run's folder
RUNNING = re.compile(r"oby-remote-gate: running in builder slot \d+")
MAC_SLOTS = 2  # the Mac worker's gate slots, oby-remote-gate's MAC_SLOTS


class Here(Exception):
    """The run stays on this Mac, for this reason."""


def word_names(command):
    """The command's words, each by the text after its last /."""
    return [word.rsplit("/", 1)[-1] for word in re.split(r"[\s;&|()<>'\"`]+", " ".join(command)) if word]


def heavy(command):
    names = word_names(command)
    if any(name in HEAVY for name in names):
        return True
    return any(name == "swift" and {"build", "test"} & set(names[i + 1 :]) for i, name in enumerate(names))


def holder():
    return LOCK.read_text(errors="replace").strip()


def remind(got, since):
    while not got.wait(REPORT_SECONDS):
        minutes = int((time.monotonic() - since) // 60)
        print(
            f"{NAME}: still waiting for the lock after {minutes} min; it is held by ({holder()})",
            file=sys.stderr,
            flush=True,
        )


def lock():
    LOCK.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(LOCK, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except BlockingIOError:
        print(f"{NAME}: another test run holds the lock ({holder()}); waiting for it", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        got = threading.Event()
        threading.Thread(target=remind, args=(got, time.monotonic()), daemon=True).start()
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        got.set()
    return fd


def environment():
    half = max(1, os.cpu_count() // 2)
    env = dict(os.environ)
    for var in CORE_VARS:
        value = env.get(var, "")
        if not (value.isdigit() and 0 < int(value) < half):
            env[var] = str(half)
    return env


def load_gate():
    """factory/bin/gate beside this copy, as a module: the macOS rule, the VM's settings, reach and uses are its."""
    path = str(Path(__file__).resolve().with_name("gate"))
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("gate", path)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader("gate", loader))
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


def git(*args, cwd=None, env=None, text=True):
    res = subprocess.run(["git", *args], cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=text, env=env)
    if res.returncode != 0:
        raise Here(f"`git {args[0]}` failed: {(res.stderr if text else res.stderr.decode(errors='replace')).strip()}")
    return res.stdout.strip() if text else res.stdout


def to_send(gate, command, vm, mac):
    """Where this run goes and what goes there, (the macOS reason for the Mac worker or None for the VM, base, tree,
    folder, payload); None to keep it here unsaid (no VM for a run that doesn't need macOS); or Here. vm and mac say
    whether the VM's and the Mac worker's builder slots are on."""
    names = word_names(command)
    said = [name for name in names if name in MAC_WORDS]
    if said:
        raise Here(f"{said[0]} runs only on a Mac")
    top = git("rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
    base = git("merge-base", "HEAD", f"origin/{gate.CONFIG['base_branch']}")
    # The worktree as it is, committed or not, untracked files too but never an ignored one, in an index of its own.
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as scratch:
        env = dict(os.environ, GIT_INDEX_FILE=os.path.join(scratch, "index"))
        git("read-tree", "HEAD", cwd=top, env=env)
        git("add", "-A", cwd=top, env=env)
        tree = git("write-tree", cwd=top, env=env)
    touched = git("diff", "--name-only", "--no-renames", base, tree, cwd=top).splitlines()
    macos = gate.macos_only(top, base, touched, tree)
    why = f"the worktree's changes touch macOS-only code: {gate.named(macos)}" if macos else None
    tests = [names[i + 1] for i, name in enumerate(names[:-1]) if name == "--test"]
    tests += [name.removeprefix("--test=") for name in names if name.startswith("--test=")]
    if tests and not why:
        listed = git("ls-tree", "-r", "--name-only", tree, "--", "core/crates", cwd=top).splitlines()
        wanted = {f"tests/{name}.rs" for name in tests}
        files = [f for f in listed if re.fullmatch(r"core/crates/[^/]+/tests/[^/]+\.rs", f)
                 and f.split("/", 3)[3] in wanted]
        macos = gate.macos_only(top, base, files, tree)
        why = f"its test is macOS-only: {gate.named(macos)}" if macos else None
    if why and not mac:
        raise Here(why)
    if not (why or vm):
        return None
    folder = os.path.relpath(os.path.realpath(os.getcwd()), os.path.realpath(top))
    if not (FOLDER.fullmatch(folder) and ".." not in folder.split("/")):
        raise Here(f"its folder, {folder}, can't be named to the {'Mac worker' if why else 'VM'}")
    if not (gate.SHA.fullmatch(base) and gate.SHA.fullmatch(tree)):
        raise Here(f"the base or the tree isn't a full SHA: {base} {tree}")
    payload = git("diff", "--binary", "--full-index", base, tree, cwd=top, text=False)
    scan = [str(gate.REPO / ".gitleaks.toml")]
    try:
        found = subprocess.run(["gitleaks", "stdin", "--config", *scan, "--no-banner", "--redact"], input=payload,
                               stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Here(f"the secret scan couldn't run: {e}")
    if found.returncode != 0:
        sys.stderr.buffer.write(found.stdout)
        raise Here(f"the secret scan found a secret in the changes, or couldn't run (gitleaks exit {found.returncode})")
    return why, base, tree, folder, payload


def send(stdin, payload):
    """The payload's size and the payload, on ssh's standard input, which then stays open (REMOTE-7)."""
    try:
        stdin.write(b"%d\n" % len(payload) + payload)
        stdin.flush()
    except OSError:
        pass


def remote_run(gate, host, user, runner, base, tree, folder, payload, command):
    """The run on the VM, or the Mac worker (user None: the one SSH logs in as), through its runner's words: its exit
    code once it started there, or gate.Fallback."""
    words = [*runner, "--wait", str(WAIT), base, tree, folder, "--", *command]
    argv = ["ssh", *gate.SSH, *(["-l", user] if user else []), host, gate.command_line(words)]
    try:
        proc = child_session.start(argv, stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
    except OSError as e:
        raise gate.Fallback(f"ssh couldn't run: {e}")
    writer = threading.Thread(target=send, args=(proc.stdin, payload), daemon=True)
    writer.start()
    ran, last = False, ""
    for line in iter(proc.stdout.readline, b""):
        sys.stdout.buffer.write(line)
        sys.stdout.buffer.flush()
        text = line.decode(errors="replace").strip()
        if not ran and text:
            ran, last = bool(RUNNING.fullmatch(text)), text
    code = proc.wait()
    writer.join(timeout=5)
    proc.stdin.close()
    code = 128 - code if code < 0 else code
    if ran:
        return code
    if last == "oby-remote-gate: all builder slots are busy":
        raise gate.Fallback(f"all builder slots were busy for {WAIT}s")
    who = f"{user}@{host}" if user else host
    raise gate.Fallback(f"ssh {who} ended {code} before the run started" + (f": {last}" if last else ""))


def on_the_vm(gate, remote, sent, command):
    """The run on the gate VM, its use open meanwhile: its exit code, or gate.Fallback."""
    use = gate.open_use()
    try:
        log, moves = [], []
        try:
            gate.reach(remote, log, moves)
        finally:
            for line in log + moves:
                print(f"{NAME}: {line}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        slots, builders = gate.sizes(remote)
        runner = ["oby-remote-gate", "--run", "--slots", str(slots), "--builder-slots", str(builders)]
        return remote_run(gate, remote["ssh_host"], remote["builder_user"], runner, *sent, command)
    finally:
        gate.close_use(use)


def on_the_mac_worker(gate, worker, why, sent, command):
    """The run on the Mac worker, in a builder slot of its own: no use, reach or probe. Its exit code, or
    gate.Fallback."""
    print(f"{NAME}: to the Mac worker {worker['ssh_host']}: {why}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
    runner = [gate.MAC_GATE, "--mac", "--run", "--slots", str(MAC_SLOTS), "--builder-slots",
              str(worker["builder_slots"])]
    return remote_run(gate, worker["ssh_host"], None, runner, *sent, command)


def elsewhere(command):
    """Run a heavy command on the gate VM, or a macOS-only one on the Mac worker: its exit code, or None to run it on
    this Mac (having said why when a builder path is on)."""
    gate = load_gate()
    remote, _ = gate.remote_config()
    worker, _ = gate.mac_worker_config()
    vm = bool(remote) and gate.sizes(remote)[1] >= 1
    mac = bool(worker) and worker["builder_slots"] >= 1
    if not (vm or mac):
        return None
    try:
        sent = to_send(gate, command, vm, mac)
    except Here as e:
        print(f"{NAME}: on this Mac: {e}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        return None
    if sent is None:
        return None
    why, *sent = sent
    try:
        return on_the_mac_worker(gate, worker, why, sent, command) if why else on_the_vm(gate, remote, sent, command)
    except gate.Fallback as e:
        print(f"{NAME}: fell back to this Mac: {e}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        return None


def main(argv):
    here = argv[1:2] == ["--here"]
    rest = argv[2:] if here else argv[1:]
    if len(rest) < 2 or rest[0] != "--":
        print(__doc__, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    command = rest[1:]
    target = os.environ.get("CARGO_TARGET_DIR")
    if target and os.path.realpath(target) == os.path.realpath(SHARED):
        print(
            f"{NAME}: CARGO_TARGET_DIR is the factory's shared Cargo folder ({SHARED}), where another worktree's"
            " build can run in place of this one's; run with CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<worktree>/core/target",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return 2
    child_session.handle_stops()
    if heavy(command):
        if here:
            print(f"{NAME}: on this Mac: the run asked for this Mac (--here)", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        code = None if here else elsewhere(command)
        if code is not None:
            return code
        fd = lock()
        started = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())
        os.ftruncate(fd, 0)
        os.pwrite(fd, f"{os.getpid()} {started} {os.getcwd()} {' '.join(command)}\n".encode(), 0)
    return child_session.run(["nice", "-n", str(PRIORITY), *command], env=environment())


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))
